  "summary": "ACCEPT. This independent plan-only review was pinned to clean candidate 0baaec6a6003b8ff055410ec39c7217d51ab1deb, correction base 7e390bf97e9564d542f6ef939349c2204a4043d5, accepted Story 12.4 dependency 4798b97d9f23aef587829175df7ab7ebc3daf995, and nonrecursive binary diff SHA-256 c69127dc1ec31adda7fe79bc7eba92b79f12a063e44c6bb5223926323e22b0b3. Checks covered Git identity/status/ancestry, exact artifact hashes, JSON parsing, 60 FR/17 SC trace rows, placeholder/stale-vocabulary scans, Constitution/PRD/BMad/August authority alignment, current source topology, and the complete immutable plan-review-07/08 findings. The corrected design is feasible and testable: one typed retrieval path makes lexical projection the sole primary authority; relationship expansion cannot rebuild primaries; deterministic top-256/12/min(3,count), deduplication and packing rules are closed; applied advisory Context is server-owned and fingerprinted; Story 12.4 many-decisions-to-one-Edge and decision-owned Published Flow Groups are preserved through a canonical complete decision set; packet 2.2 and absent/present-valid/present-inconsistent/selected-required states are closed; B1-B4 interaction REDs guard the cutover; conversation is transient and revalidated; mandatory raw streaming, whole-answer validation, accepted-only reveal and neutral Track B telemetry are separate from Track C attestation. FR-054/SC-015 are now consistent across plan, data model, streaming contract and release evidence: one nonterminal SSE data event is one received Provider Chunk; exact data-value wire UTF-8 bytes are bounded at 16,384 before JSON decoding, their assembled received-response sum is bounded at 65,536 before JSON, and raw-body/SSE plus decoded-delta/final-answer limits retain independent counters, exact/+1/escape/metadata/precedence tests and signed release recomputation. No alternate authority path, Critical/High finding, Constitution/PRD conflict, Story 12.4 mutation, EF migration, VulgataDbContext/snapshot change, or Track C execution is authorized. The sole Low finding is stale specification lifecycle metadata and does not block this gate. Planned-change determination: Agent-tool/material Chat retrieval and provider-dispatch change YES; Scan-strategy change NO; PRD conflict/weakening NO. A fresh explicit planned-change authorization is therefore required before regenerated tasks; prior tasks are stale/excluded, Track A remains preserved, and Track C remains closed."
